      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(init): select authenticated X account",
        "body": "Fresh BirdClaw databases currently keep the demo `@steipete` identity even when xurl is authenticated as someone else. That sends the first sync toward the wrong account unless the database is repaired manually.\n\nThis change makes `birdclaw init` adopt the authenticated xurl identity and adds `--account <username>` for users with multiple OAuth2 accounts. It persists the selected handle and X user ID, while only replacing the untouched demo seed so imported archive ownership remains safe.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `pnpm test` — 1,276 tests passed\n- `pnpm check` — formatting, lint, and TypeScript passed\n- Added regression coverage for explicit OAuth2 selection, external user ID persistence, CLI option forwarding, and preservation of imported accounts\n\n## Post-Deploy Monitoring & Validation\n\nNo deployment-specific monitoring is needed. Validate with a fresh database by running `birdclaw init --account <username>` and confirming the returned account matches the selected authenticated xurl identity.\n\n---\n\n[![Compound Engineering](https://img.shields.io/badge/Built_with-Compound_Engineering-6366f1)](https://github.com/EveryInc/compound-engineering-plugin)\n![Codex](https://img.shields.io/badge/GPT--5-Codex-111827?logo=openai&logoColor=white)\n",
